<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, Al–taschith, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song of Asaph.</title><sup><b>1</b></sup> Unto thee, O God, do we give thanks, <i>unto thee</i> do we give thanks: for <i>that</i> thy name is near thy wondrous works declare.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, Al–taschith, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song of Asaph.</title><sup><b>2</b></sup> When I shall receive the congregation I will judge uprightly.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, Al–taschith, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song of Asaph.</title><sup><b>3</b></sup> The earth and all the inhabitants thereof are dissolved: I bear up the pillars of it. Selah.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, Al–taschith, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song of Asaph.</title><sup><b>4</b></sup> I said unto the fools, Deal not foolishly: and to the wicked, Lift not up the horn:<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, Al–taschith, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song of Asaph.</title><sup><b>5</b></sup> Lift not up your horn on high: speak <i>not with</i> a stiff neck.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, Al–taschith, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song of Asaph.</title><sup><b>6</b></sup> For promotion <i>cometh</i> neither from the east, nor from the west, nor from the south.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, Al–taschith, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song of Asaph.</title><sup><b>7</b></sup> But God <i>is</i> the judge: he putteth down one, and setteth up another.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, Al–taschith, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song of Asaph.</title><sup><b>8</b></sup> For in the hand of the LORD <i>there is</i> a cup, and the wine is red; it is full of mixture; and he poureth out of the same: but the dregs thereof, all the wicked of the earth shall wring <i>them</i> out, <i>and</i> drink <i>them</i>.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, Al–taschith, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song of Asaph.</title><sup><b>9</b></sup> But I will declare for ever; I will sing praises to the God of Jacob.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician, Al–taschith, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song of Asaph.</title><sup><b>10</b></sup> All the horns of the wicked also will I cut off; <i>but</i> the horns of the righteous shall be exalted. <br />
